  "body": "Clean up color conversion presentation in HTML canvas\n\nThe \"Color spaces and color space conversion\" section contains the following text that needs adjustment:\n* \"When drawing content to a 2D context, all inputs must be converted to the context's color space before drawing.\"\n  * This logic affects the \"Drawing model\" algorithm, so move it there\n* \"Alpha blending must be performed on values after conversion to the context's color space.\"\n  * This logic, too, affects the \"Drawing model\" algorithm, so move it there\n* \"Interpolation of gradient color stops must be performed on color values after conversion to the context's color space\"\n  * This logic affects the gradient stops algorithm in the \"Fill and stroke styles\" section, so move it there\n\nThe `PredefinedColorSpace` enum is defined in the \"The 2D rendering context\" section\n* This is also used extensively by the WebGL and WebGPU rendering contexts as well\n  * Move the this into the \"Color spaces and color space conversion\" instead\n\nCouple of additional thoughts:\n* I would also be fine moving the `PredefinedColorSpace` to the \"The canvas element\" section, and just deleting \"Color spaces and color space conversion\". It may be that we will want that section to exist for tone mapping, etc, in the future, which is my motivation for defaulting to leaving it here.\n* The treatment of the bitmap of the canvas and the bitmap of the rendering context and the bitmap of 2D rendering contexts, could be cleaned up (there is no \"concept\" for the first two). I'm intentionally not touching that issue here, since it will likely need a more extensive treatment.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/11601/canvas.html\" title=\"Last updated on Sep 15, 2025, 11:27 AM UTC (b8c8226)\">/canvas.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/11601/56a15bf...b8c8226/canvas.html\" title=\"Last updated on Sep 15, 2025, 11:27 AM UTC (b8c8226)\">diff</a> )",
